  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{6}$ from ${a}_{7}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{7}-{a}_{6} \\\\  & =11-6 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
